vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] cipherSuite https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/install-splunk-enterprise-securely/about-tls-encryption-and-cipher-suites
vendor:          web.conf [settings] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
# --- end vendor verification

external:        FIPS mode is enabled at install time; the SPLK-CL-000390 fix text states
                 that enabling it afterward requires a reinstall or upgrade of the
                 application - installation procedure
external:        The validated cryptographic module itself and kernel FIPS mode on the host
                 - operating system and the OpenSSL FIPS module
external:        Identification of which data is compartmentalized and therefore requires
                 cryptographic protection - organizational policy, which the check text
                 directs be read from policy documents
external:        The approved cipher string and TLS profile for the environment -
                 organization-defined value
external:        Operation in the Common Criteria evaluated configuration, which
                 splunk-launch.conf SPLUNK_COMMON_CRITERIA selects: it is an evaluation
                 posture rather than the cryptographic-module control this requirement asks
                 for, and SPLUNK_FIPS carries that control on the same requirement.

citation:        Product STIG SPLK-CL-000390 fix text, which adds SPLUNK_COMMON_CRITERIA=1
                 and SPLUNK_FIPS=1 to splunk-launch.conf before the initial start of Splunk
                 Enterprise, and whose check text verifies "splunk show fips-mode" returns
                 FIPS mode enabled; splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-116 (SPLUNK_FIPS = [0|1]);
                 server.conf.spec:1005-1006 (Common Criteria mode is a documented operating
                 mode: "If you run Splunk Enterprise in Common Criteria mode, then you must
                 give this setting a value"); server.conf.spec:714 ([sslConfig]) with
                 :765-778 (sslVersions = <comma-separated list>; available versions ssl3,
                 tls1.0, tls1.1, tls1.2; "*" selects all supported versions and "tls"
                 selects all versions tls1.0 or newer; a "-" prefix excludes a version),
                 :940 (cipherSuite), :996-1009 (sslRootCAPath, no default);
                 web.conf.spec:239-245 (sslVersions, same vocabulary), :255-261
                 (cipherSuite; "If not set, uses the default cipher string provided by
                 OpenSSL")
finding:         Cryptographic protections are not configured to the extent the product
                 allows: FIPS or Common Criteria mode is not enabled, a TLS version list
                 selects a protocol below TLS 1.2 or uses a wildcard that admits one, a
                 cipher string is left to the library default, or the root certificate
                 authority path required in Common Criteria mode is unset.
